WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:01.490
OK, now, one other thing.

00:00:01.490 --> 00:00:06.480
I want to separate this clip out from yesterday's
press briefing, because it really boggles

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:13.370
the mind how ignorant and clueless Donald
Trump still is on the basics of Corona virus

00:00:13.370 --> 00:00:15.269
during yesterday's press briefing.

00:00:15.269 --> 00:00:21.590
Donald Trump asked, is there a way to separate
the flu and corona virus?

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:28.230
Can we distinguish if someone has the flu
from someone who has corona virus?

00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:35.140
It's almost like Trump hasn't spent the last
six months talking about testing Corona virus

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:42.789
testing corona virus tests, which tell you
whether you have corona virus or not.

00:00:42.789 --> 00:00:48.629
This is inconceivable that this is a question
we're still getting from Trump in September.

00:00:48.629 --> 00:00:50.049
You see what's happening in Europe.

00:00:50.049 --> 00:00:52.609
However, they have a very big spike.

00:00:52.609 --> 00:00:55.039
Countries that we thought we're doing well
aren't doing well.

00:00:55.039 --> 00:00:58.659
They had some very big spikes, very, very
big surge.

00:00:58.659 --> 00:01:05.930
Months ago, we increased our nation's procurement
of the flu vaccine by 66 percent.

00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:10.060
And we ask Americans to go get their annual
flu shot as early as possible.

00:01:10.060 --> 00:01:17.409
It's possible, I would imagine, Scott, that
the flu can get mixed up with the virus and

00:01:17.409 --> 00:01:21.329
people can they get the virus when actually
it's another flu season coming on?

00:01:21.329 --> 00:01:22.820
I don't know.

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:23.820
It's.

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:24.979
I hope they can keep them separate.

00:01:24.979 --> 00:01:26.439
Can they keep them separate?

00:01:26.439 --> 00:01:28.359
We hope so.

00:01:28.359 --> 00:01:29.640
They will.

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:31.640
It's going to be a very interesting time.

00:01:31.640 --> 00:01:33.490
But we have a flu season coming up.

00:01:33.490 --> 00:01:38.729
We've had some flu seasons, which are really
massive over the years.

00:01:38.729 --> 00:01:43.979
Scott, do we have a way of separating a flu
case and a corona virus case?

00:01:43.979 --> 00:01:45.170
And even more bizarre.

00:01:45.170 --> 00:01:46.829
I mean, it's a Gong Show.

00:01:46.829 --> 00:01:50.289
Scott Atlus bizarrely says, I hope we do.

00:01:50.289 --> 00:01:53.479
And Donald Trump says, I don't think we do.

00:01:53.479 --> 00:01:58.810
He's spent the last six to seven months talking
about Corona virus tests, testing how many

00:01:58.810 --> 00:02:00.899
tests, how fast are the tests?

00:02:00.899 --> 00:02:02.210
He says it all the time.

00:02:02.210 --> 00:02:04.749
When you test, you find cases.

00:02:04.749 --> 00:02:08.130
That's how you separate a corona virus case
from something else.

00:02:08.130 --> 00:02:12.030
We have a test for the flu, which tells us
if someone has the flu.

00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:16.260
We have a test for corona virus, which tells
us if someone has corona virus.

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:19.459
How does the president of the United States
not know that at this point?

00:02:19.459 --> 00:02:25.200
It it's a mind blowing, inconceivable ignorance
and and maybe more import.

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:30.650
Well, not more importantly, but equally interesting
is that this is probably a peek behind the

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:34.290
curtain of how people deal with Trump behind
the scenes.

00:02:34.290 --> 00:02:38.050
The normal response, if someone says, hey,
can we tell the difference between corona

00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:39.050
virus and the flu?

00:02:39.050 --> 00:02:41.820
A normal response would be absolutely.

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:44.230
We have tests for the flu and we have test
for corona virus.

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:45.230
No problem.

00:02:45.230 --> 00:02:46.430
This is how it works.

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:50.150
Scott Atlas instead says, I hope that we can
wait.

00:02:50.150 --> 00:02:52.930
And my sense is that this is how it works
behind the scenes.

00:02:52.930 --> 00:03:00.010
Frequently we wonder Trump spin mispronouncing
convalescent plasma as convalescent plasma

00:03:00.010 --> 00:03:01.100
for months.

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:03.530
How is no one just said, you know Mr. Pratt,
sir.

00:03:03.530 --> 00:03:06.450
As Trump likes to say, sir, it's plasma.

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:09.720
Apparently, Trump loses his mind when people
do that.

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:13.812
We wonder why does Trump keep saying the 1917
flu?

00:03:13.812 --> 00:03:15.150
It's the 1918 flu.

00:03:15.150 --> 00:03:18.849
Why has no one gone up to him and said it's
1918, not 1917?

00:03:18.849 --> 00:03:24.110
Well, Scott Atlas's response tells us why
people are either afraid of Trump or they've

00:03:24.110 --> 00:03:29.330
decided they can't correct him or it's pointless
to correct him or whatever.

00:03:29.330 --> 00:03:32.489
But that is probably the explanation that
you saw there.

00:03:32.489 --> 00:03:37.510
It and it's scary because there is no error
correcting mechanism in the same way that

00:03:37.510 --> 00:03:42.860
Scott Atlas doesn't just say, yes, of course,
we have flu tests and coronavirus tests.

00:03:42.860 --> 00:03:48.260
We have to believe that behind the scenes
you see a similar lack of pushback on foreign

00:03:48.260 --> 00:03:51.819
policy, on economic policy, on everything.

00:03:51.819 --> 00:05:03.820
Horrifying, horrifying

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:04.720
and frightening.

